<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Chikhori (1757)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1757</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Chikhori was fought in 1757 in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, where King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon-i-of-imereti">Solomon I of Imereti</a> defeated an Ottoman army supporting his rebellious nobles. The victory strengthened his hold on the kingdom against Ottoman-backed rivals, and he went on to ban the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a> from Imereti, which had long supplied the Ottoman market with captives.</p></div>
